# LF in this tree, whatever the desk that clones it has set. Without this file the answer comes
# from the cloning desk's core.autocrlf, which on the desk Studio was written on is true: a fresh
# clone landed tools/pre-commit at 14553 bytes against the blob's 14263, 290 carriage returns the
# repository does not hold. Git for Windows' sh runs such a hook anyway, which is why it went
# unseen; a POSIX sh reads the shebang's trailing CR as part of the interpreter's name.
#
# tests/eol-attrs.mjs reads these attributes out of the INDEX and refuses any tracked file that
# leaves the question open, so a file added later inherits the rule rather than the habit.
* text=auto eol=lf
# No binary is tracked here yet. One added later says so on its own line, because text=auto is a
# detection and a detection is a guess: a fixture holding one NUL byte reads as binary and stops
# being converted at all, silently.

# The one binary tracked here: the app icon, a copy of etiuda-logo/studio/etiuda-app.ico. `-text` is
# `text` unset, which tests/eol-attrs.mjs accepts as "declared binary, no conversion"; without
# the line the answer comes from text=auto's detection, and a detection is a guess.
*.ico -text
